diff --git a/manual/playbooks/accounts-quota.md b/manual/playbooks/accounts-quota.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fcc3fc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/accounts-quota.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+id: accounts-quota
+title: Use several accounts and stay within quota
+area: accounts
+summary: Capture sign-ins, see room per account, pick accounts per run or by rule, move a live conversation, and set handover thresholds.
+intents:
+  - use my second claude account
+  - which account has room
+  - rotate accounts for long runs
+  - switch this conversation to another account
+keywords: [account, accounts, quota, rotate, second account, switch account, limit, room, sign in]
+ops: [accounts.list, accounts.status, accounts.capture, accounts.activate, policies.list, console.setAccount, sessions.contextGuard]
+---
+## Steps
+- Room now: `accounts.status engine=claude`; all slots: `accounts.list`.
+- Add a sign-in: the user logs in with the engine's own login, then `accounts.capture engine=claude label="<label>"`.
+- Per run: pass `account=<slot id>` or a rule (`@emptiest`, `@round-robin`, names in `policies.list`) on `tasks.add`, `console.start`, `schedules.add`, `missions.start`...
+- Next sessions by default: `accounts.activate id=<slot>`; per agent: `agents.defaults.set agent=<a> engine=<e> account=<slot>`.
+- Move a live Console conversation: `console.setAccount id=<card> account=<slot or rule>` (from the next message).
+- Long work across accounts: a baton relay with an account pool (playbook baton-relay).
+- Handover thresholds (context and quota): `sessions.contextGuard`; change only on request.
diff --git a/manual/playbooks/backlog-work.md b/manual/playbooks/backlog-work.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1292bc8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/backlog-work.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: backlog-work
+title: Work with a project backlog (add, order, pick next, close)
+area: projects
+summary: Add items with the right origin, see what is startable next, reorder, hold, and learn how an item was handled before.
+intents:
+  - add this to the backlog
+  - what should I work on next
+  - do the top five backlog items
+  - move K-7 after S-2
+  - how was this solved last time
+keywords: [backlog, item, next, priority, order, queue, hold, park, code, add item, history of item]
+ops: [projects.backlog, projects.backlog.next, projects.backlog.add, projects.backlog.reorder, projects.backlog.move, projects.backlog.hold, projects.backlog.check, projects.tracks]
+---
+## Steps
+- What to do next (startable items in queue order; blocked and held ones listed apart): `projects.backlog.next project=<p> limit=5`.
+- Add an item. Mark `origin=user` when the user asked for it; your own proposals keep the default:
+```json
+{ "op": "projects.backlog.add", "args": { "project": "<p>", "text": "<item text>", "area": "K", "priority": "high", "effort": "S", "origin": "user" } }
+```
+- Reorder: `projects.backlog.reorder` (before or after another item) or `projects.backlog.move` (up, down, top, bottom). Park: `projects.backlog.hold`.
+- Before starting an item, read its history: `projects.tracks project=<p> code=<K-n>`.
+- Start and finish: `projects.backlog.check ... state=doing`, later `state=done note="..."` (playbook project-session-close).
diff --git a/manual/playbooks/baton-relay.md b/manual/playbooks/baton-relay.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ef17f1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/baton-relay.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: baton-relay
+title: Start a baton relay chain (long work that survives quota and context limits)
+area: relay
+summary: Open a relay so a long job continues in fresh sessions across accounts when a leg reaches its quota or context line; then control the chain.
+intents:
+  - start a baton chain for this job
+  - keep working on this overnight until it is finished
+  - run this as a relay across my accounts
+  - make this session a relay
+  - continue this in a new session when the limit hits
+keywords: [baton, relay, chain, overnight, continue, keep going, marathon, legs, accounts, handover]
+ops: [agents.list, accounts.status, policies.list, tasks.add, console.start, baton.attach, chains.list, baton.legs, baton.setLegs, chains.pause, chains.resume, chains.end, baton.stop]
+effect: run
+---
+## Ask only if missing
+The job and the agent; how many legs at most (`maxHops`, 0 = no ceiling; the default comes from settings); which account pool (default `@emptiest`); whether the legs run headless, in the Console or in a terminal.
+
+## Steps
+1. `agents.list`; `accounts.status engine=claude` to see room; `policies.list` if the user named a rule.
+2. Open the chain with its first leg. Headless (file payload):
+```json
+{ "op": "tasks.add", "args": { "agent": "<agent>", "title": "<job> (relay)", "prompt": "<the whole job, what done means, and: commit after every atomic step>", "baton": true, "maxHops": 8, "account": "@emptiest", "permissionMode": "acceptEdits" } }
+```
+   In the Console instead: `console.start` with the same `agent`, `prompt`, `baton=true`, `maxHops`, `account`.
+   An already running session (for example your own): `baton.attach` (default: the caller) with `maxHops` and `account`.
+3. Confirm: `chains.list` shows the chain; `baton.legs chain=<chn_id>` lists legs as they open.
+
+## Control (on the user's word)
+- More or fewer legs: `baton.setLegs chain=<id> maxLegs=N` (or `add=2`).
+- Pause: `chains.pause chain=<id> mode=pass` (the next leg waits at the door) or `mode=here` (short break in the same session); continue with `chains.resume chain=<id>`.
+- End: `chains.end chain=<id>` (the running leg writes its note instead of passing); stop a waiting successor: `baton.stop chain=<id> why="..."`.
+
+## Pitfalls
+- Each leg is a paid session; a chain can run for hours.
+- Each firing of a schedule or trigger with `baton=true` opens its own chain.
+- A chain stops by itself after two legs in a row without a new commit (barren brake): the prompt must make legs commit.
