new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c16d6e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/multi-step-workflow.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+---
+id: multi-step-workflow
+title: Chain agents step by step (workflow)
+area: workflows
+summary: Create and run a workflow whose steps run in order, each reading the previous step's output, with optional conditions, checks and inputs.
+intents:
+  - first the writer drafts, then the editor fixes it
+  - make a pipeline research then summarize then translate
+  - create a workflow with these steps
+  - run the weekly content workflow
+keywords: [workflow, pipeline, chain, steps, then, after, handoff, sequence]
+ops: [agents.list, workflows.recipes, workflows.add, workflows.list, workflows.run, workflows.status, workflows.resume]
+effect: write
+---
+## Steps
+1. `agents.list` for exact names; `workflows.recipes` if a ready-made recipe fits (`workflows.addRecipe`).
+2. Create (file payload). Each step reads the previous one with `{prev_text}` (its text) or `{prev_output}` (its output file path); declared inputs are `{input.<name>}`:
+```json
+{ "op": "workflows.add", "args": { "title": "Draft and edit", "inputs": [ { "name": "topic", "required": true } ], "steps": [ { "agent": "<writer>", "title": "Draft", "prompt": "Write a draft about {input.topic}." }, { "agent": "<editor>", "title": "Edit", "prompt": "Edit this draft for clarity and correctness:\n{prev_text}", "onFail": "stop" } ] } }
+```
+   Options per step: `engine`, `model`, `runIf` (regex on the previous output), `onFail` (stop, continue or a step number), `verify` ({criteria, retries}), `outputContract=json` then `{prev_json.field}` downstream, `forEach` to fan out over a list.
+3. Run only when the user wants it now: `workflows.run id=<title> inputs={"topic": "..."}` → run id.
+4. Follow: `workflows.status runId=<id>`. A broken run resumes at the failed step: `workflows.resume taskId=<that step's task id>`.
+
+## Tell the user
+Title, steps, inputs, how to run it again, and (when run) the run id and outcome.
+
+## Pitfalls
+- Each agent step is a paid run.
+- To run on a timer or a file event, use a trigger with `action=workflow` (playbook react-to-events).
diff --git a/manual/playbooks/notify-user.md b/manual/playbooks/notify-user.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ffbe20
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/notify-user.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: notify-user
+title: Tell the user something, deliver a report, or ask a question (Notices)
+area: notices
+summary: Post one well-formed notice (with an optional full report) to the user's Notices board, or leave an asynchronous question.
+intents:
+  - let me know when it is done
+  - send me a report
+  - notify the user
+  - leave me a question
+  - remind me
+  - post a warning
+keywords: [notify, notice, tell, report, message, question, reminder, warning, result, summary]
+ops: [notices.post, notices.edit, notices.dismiss, notices.list, notices.resolve]
+effect: write
+---
+## When
+The user is not reading this chat (unattended run, task, schedule) or asked to be told on the board. In a live chat, just answer in the chat.
+
+## Steps
+1. Choose `type` (update, report, result, reminder, suggestion, warning, question) and an honest `level` (1 routine, 2 medium, 3 important, 4 critical).
+2. Write one notice. Summary in `body`; parts in `sections`; the full text in `report` (saved to the report folder and linked):
+```json
+{ "op": "notices.post", "args": { "title": "Weekly research digest ready", "type": "report", "level": 2, "agent": "<you>", "body": "<3-6 line summary a reader understands without opening the report>", "report": "<full markdown report with sources at the end>", "reportName": "weekly-research-digest" } }
+```
+   Call `notices.post @notice.json` and keep the returned id.
+3. For a question: `"type": "question"`; check for the answer later (playbook check-inbox), act, then `notices.resolve id=<id>`.
+
+## Pitfalls
+- One thing = one notice; never one per sub-item.
+- Never re-post to read an answer you cut off: an identical post within 10 minutes is refused and the first one is returned. Fix with `notices.edit`; withdraw with `notices.dismiss`.
+- Write user-facing text in the user's language (`farm.brief` reports it).
