@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: sentry-campaign
+title: Work through a project backlog unattended (sentry campaign)
+area: sentry
+summary: Start, watch, pause and stop a sentry campaign that opens unattended rounds on a project's backlog items across accounts.
+intents:
+  - work through the backlog overnight
+  - start the night shift on this project
+  - keep taking backlog items until I stop you
+keywords: [sentry, night shift, overnight, backlog, unattended, campaign, autonomous]
+ops: [projects.backlog.next, accounts.status, sentry.start, sentry.status, sentry.pause, sentry.resume, sentry.stop]
+effect: run
+---
+## Ask only if missing
+Project, agent, engine, the opening instruction, and the brakes the user accepts (failure limit, account ceiling). Make sure they know it runs until stopped.
+
+## Steps
+1. `projects.backlog.next project=<p>` — what it would take first; `accounts.status engine=<e>` — room.
+2. Start:
+```json
+{ "op": "sentry.start", "args": { "project": "<project>", "agent": "<agent>", "engine": "claude", "prompt": "<how to work an item: take the next startable backlog item, implement, test, commit, close it with a note>", "permissionMode": "acceptEdits", "preset": "hybrid", "failLimit": 3 } }
+```
+   Rounds that must write outside their own folder need `permissionMode=bypassPermissions`, only if the user accepts it.
+3. Watch: `sentry.status` (what it does and why).
+4. Pause, resume, stop on the user's word: `sentry.pause`, `sentry.resume`, `sentry.stop why="..."` (a running round continues; cancel it with `tasks.cancel` if asked).
diff --git a/manual/playbooks/standing-duty.md b/manual/playbooks/standing-duty.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82c14a9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/standing-duty.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: standing-duty
+title: Make an agent keep watching something (standing duty)
+area: agents
+summary: Record a duty in the agent's DUTIES.md and wire an automation behind it so it actually happens while the agent is idle.
+intents:
+  - keep an eye on this folder and process new files
+  - every morning check the inbox and triage it
+  - watch for new issues and tell me
+  - make this a standing duty of the assistant
+keywords: [duty, duties, watch, keep an eye, monitor, standing, routine, every turn]
+ops: [duties.add, duties.automate, duties.list, schedules.add]
+effect: write
+---
+## Model
+A duty in `DUTIES.md` (`## Title [cadence]`, Watch, Do) is read by the agent while it runs. Cadences: every-turn, session-start, daily, weekly, manual. A daily or weekly duty with no automation behind it never happens; an every-turn duty only runs while the agent is already running.
+
+## Steps
+1. Record it:
+```json
+{ "op": "duties.add", "args": { "agent": "<agent>", "title": "Inbox triage", "cadence": "daily", "watch": "<folder>", "do": "File each new note into the right folder and log it." } }
+```
+2. Wire it, in the same move:
+   - Latency matters: `duties.automate agent=<agent> title="Inbox triage"` (a watch trigger; needs a real path).
+   - Otherwise (usually better): a daily schedule with a precondition that names the duty (playbook recurring-task), `fireIf {kind: folderHasFiles, path: <folder>}`.
+3. Check: `duties.list agent=<agent>` shows the duty with its live watch status.
+
+## Pitfalls
+A folder watch fires on any change: prefer a daily batch with `fireIf` unless the user needs quick reaction.
