@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+---
+id: start-session
+title: Open a conversation with an agent (Console or terminal)
+area: console
+summary: Start an interactive session for the user or a Console card you drive, send messages, and hand it back.
+intents:
+  - open a session with the designer
+  - start talking to agent X
+  - open claude for the backend agent
+  - send this message to that session
+keywords: [session, console, chat, talk, conversation, open, terminal]
+ops: [agents.list, console.start, console.send, console.sessions, console.answer, sessions.start]
+effect: run
+---
+## Choose
+- The user will talk to it themselves in a terminal: `sessions.start agent=<a>` (`surface=console` for the panel, `engine`, `model`, `prompt`, `resume=<sessionId>` to continue).
+- You will drive it (send messages, read answers): `console.start`.
+
+## Steps (Console)
+1. `agents.list` for the exact agent name.
+2. Start it, with the first message in a file:
+```json
+{ "op": "console.start", "args": { "agent": "<agent>", "prompt": "<first message>", "engine": "claude" } }
+```
+   Keep the returned console `id`.
+3. Follow: `console.sessions id=<id> messages=5`. If it is `asking` a question, answer only what the user decided: `console.answer id=<id> response="..."`. Permission prompts are the user's.
+4. Next message: `console.send id=<id> text="..."` (held until the turn ends on engines other than Claude).
+
+## Tell the user
+Which agent, engine and card; they can open it with "Agent Farm: Open Console".
+
+## Pitfalls
+- Each message is a paid turn.
+- One card per session: resuming a session that already has a card returns that card.
diff --git a/manual/playbooks/stop-things.md b/manual/playbooks/stop-things.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..004445e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/manual/playbooks/stop-things.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+---
+id: stop-things
+title: Stop, pause or cancel anything safely
+area: basics
+summary: The right op to stop each kind of work, what survives, and how to pause instead of destroy.
+intents:
+  - stop everything
+  - cancel that task
+  - stop the mission
+  - pause all automations
+  - stop the relay chain
+  - interrupt the session
+keywords: [stop, cancel, pause, halt, interrupt, kill, end, abort, brake]
+ops: [tasks.cancel, console.interrupt, sessions.interrupt, sessions.end, missions.pause, missions.cancel, chains.pause, chains.end, baton.stop, workflows.decide, automations.pause, sentry.pause, sentry.stop]
+effect: destructive
+---
+## Pick the narrowest stop
+| What | Pause (keeps state) | Stop |
+|---|---|---|
+| A task | — | `tasks.cancel id=<id>` |
+| A Console turn | — | `console.interrupt id=<card>` (conversation survives) |
+| A terminal session's turn | — | `sessions.interrupt sessionId=<id>`; end the process: `sessions.end` (asks the user) |
+| A mission | `missions.pause id=<run>` | `missions.cancel id=<run>` |
+| A relay chain | `chains.pause chain=<id> mode=pass` | `chains.end chain=<id>`, or `baton.stop chain=<id>` for a waiting successor |
+| A running workflow | `workflows.decide runId=<id> decision=stop` | — |
+| All schedules and triggers | `automations.pause minutes=<n> reason="..."` | `automations.bulk set=off` |
+| The sentry campaign | `sentry.pause` | `sentry.stop` |
+
+## Rules
+- "Stop everything" from the user: pause automations first, then list what runs (`now.get`, `tasks.list`, `missions.list`, `chains.list`) and confirm before cancelling running work.
+- Nothing here deletes history; say what was stopped and how to resume.
